            text: "\nWe protect data with access controls and encryption in transit, and we keep improving our protections and fixing weaknesses we find. No system is perfectly secure.\n\n**Where your data is stored.** Tuturuuu is based in Vietnam. We store and process data with the providers listed in the [Subprocessor Registry](/legal/subprocessors). Our primary databases and file storage are hosted outside Vietnam (in Singapore and the wider Asia-Pacific region). Our team's devices in Vietnam may access and temporarily hold data for support and operations. Some providers do not let us choose the country: for example, Google may process or briefly store data sent to its Gemini API in any country where it has facilities. Under Vietnamese law, this is a transfer of personal data abroad. The registry gives general location information for each provider.\n\n**Transfers from the EU or UK.** Vietnam has no EU or UK adequacy decision. Where we receive data from the EU or UK, we rely on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses, with the UK Addendum for UK data, as set out in our [DPA](/legal/dpa); our providers rely on the transfer terms in their own data processing agreements, which the registry names where we have checked them. You can ask for a copy at legal@tuturuuu.com.\n\n**Security incidents and personal data breaches.** A security incident is an event that may affect our systems or the data in them. A personal data breach is a security incident in which personal data was, or may have been, accessed, disclosed, altered, lost or destroyed without authorisation. We triage first alerts within 24 hours. We are aware of a personal data breach once we reasonably believe that personal data was or may have been affected. We assess each incident in parallel with the notice deadlines below, and the assessment never pauses them: if we have not ruled out that personal data was exposed by the earliest deadline, we send a preliminary notice and complete it later.\n- **Data that belongs to an organisation that uses Tuturuuu:** we tell that organisation without undue delay and within 24 hours of becoming aware of the breach, so that it can meet its own duties.\n- **Data we control:** where Vietnamese law requires it, we notify Vietnam's specialised personal data protection agency at the Ministry of Public Security (Department of Cybersecurity and High-Tech Crime Prevention, A05) within 72 hours, as Article 23(1) of the Law on Personal Data Protection No. 91/2025/QH15 and Decree No. 356/2025/ND-CP require. We count the 72 hours from the earlier of when we detect the violation and when we become aware of the breach. We tell the people affected where the law requires it.\n- **Compliance incidents without data exposure** are logged. Where Vietnamese law requires it, for example when personal data was processed for a purpose or in a way that was not agreed, we notify the authority (Law No. 91/2025/QH15, Article 23(3)) and tell the customers concerned.\n\n",
